cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the HeritageGraph ontology, please cite it as below."
title: "HeritageGraph Ontology"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-07-16"
authors:
  - name: "CAIR-Nepal"
    website: "https://cair-nepal.org"
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/CAIRNepal/heritagegraphontology"
url: "https://w3id.org/heritagegraph/ontology"
abstract: >-
  An event-centric LinkML schema for representing cultural heritage
  information of the Kathmandu Valley, aligned with CIDOC-CRM and PROV-O
  through exact/broad mappings and subproperty bridges. Covers tangible and
  living heritage including temples, stupas, water architecture, rituals,
  festivals, Guthi institutions, and the Kumari (living goddess) lifecycle,
  with a CRMinf-based layer for contested, source-attributed assertions.
keywords:
  - ontology
  - cultural heritage
  - CIDOC-CRM
  - PROV-O
  - LinkML
  - Nepal
  - living heritage
